 "seat": "implementation",
 "instruction": "Add trace logging to `TurboManager` (`sanctuary/core/turbo.py`), to support tuning its thresholds from real data.\n\n- New constructor parameter `trace_path: Optional[Path] = None`.\n- When it's set, every `observe()` call appends one JSON line to that file with these fields:\n  - `t`: the observe time\n  - `per_source`: each source's intensity, keyed by the source's `name`\n  - `intensity`: the aggregate\n  - `dominant_source`\n  - `state_before` and `state_after`: the state enum values, like \"idle\", \"armed\", \"active\"\n  - `current_rate_hz`: the controller's current rate\n  - `is_turbo_active`\n- Create the file's parent directories as needed. Tracing is best-effort: a write failure is logged and otherwise ignored, and must never affect the cognitive cycle. With no trace path, no file is created.\n- Add `turbo_trace_path: Optional[str] = None` to `RunnerConfig` in `sanctuary/api/runner.py`, and pass it through when the runner builds its `TurboManager`.",
